      "entity": "Johnnie",
      "scope": "main character",
      "claim": "Johnnie is the central figure in the narrative of \"The Lost Prince,\" as he is the subject of the King's deathbed summons, the funeral, the medical diagnosis, and the decision to send him to Sandringham.",
      "answer": "Johnnie",
      "quote": "a glimpse of an approaching comet, Johnnie's parents are called to Buckingham Palace to be by the King's deathbed. During the funeral attended by all the heads of state of Europe, including the Kaiser Wilhelm, Johnnie succumbs to a serious epileptic fit. Queen Mary, Johnnie's mother, summons doctors to examine him and their diagnosis confirms her and Lalla's worst fears. Lalla volunteers to look after Johnnie to prevent him being sent to an institution.",
